// A repeated hole on a rule's left-hand side: refused at the cell layer's
// admission boundary, with the copy named.
//
// Cell patterns are linear (circuit-terms-question-17): a metavariable that
// occurs twice on a left-hand side is a copy on a wire, and a copy needs a
// comonoid the type may not have. `rule and(x, x) ==> x` — idempotence written
// with a repeated hole — elaborates to a cut whose producer hole `x` occurs
// twice, so the admission boundary refuses the cell, and the diagnostic names
// the copy and the respelling: match through the copying cell, exactly as a
// fan-in cell must name its monoid. A type supplying a cocommutative comonoid
// may host the copy explicitly — the named later generalization
// (circuit-terms-question-18), not a shape this store admits today.
//
// The refusal is decline-and-report, not abort: the linear companion rule
// still lands. Three cells reach the store — the two constructor frames and
// the linear rule — and the copying rule is the one decline.
data Bit : Type {
  Off : Bit;
  On : Bit;
  oper and(a : Bit, b : Bit) -> Bit;
  rule and(x, y) ==> y;
  rule and(x, x) ==> x;
}

//@ mode: desc
//@ expect-desc-rules: 2
//@ expect-desc-store-cells: 3
//@ expect-desc-cell-decline: the producer hole `x` occurs more than once
